<mod:findName type = "event" name = "NEMESIS_ENCOUNTER">
	<mod-append:choice req="LIST_CREW_LEAH" max_group="666" hidden="true" blue="true">
	<text>(Leah) Use Leah to hail the ship.</text>
	<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH"/>
	</mod-append:choice>
</mod:findName>

<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH">
	<loadEventList seeded="true" generate="true">
		<event name="LEAH_LIST_NEMESIS_LEAH"/>
	</loadEventList>
</event>

<eventList name="LEAH_LIST_NEMESIS_LEAH">
	<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_MIMIC"/>
	<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WHO_IS_WHO"/>
	<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_CREW"/>
	<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_CREW"/>
	<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WEAPON"/>
	<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WEAPON"/>
	<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SCRAP"/>
	<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SCRAP"/>
</eventList>

<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_MIMIC" unique="true">
	<ship load="SHIP_NEMESIS" hostile="true"/>
	<text>The captain hails you, revealing themselves to have obnoxiously bright blue hair and a smug glare. "Didn't expect to see m- wait, WHAT!? That's me!? I'm on your ship, but I haven't even teleported over yet!" The rebel ship's communications go blank, but then you hear a 'FWOOP' as their captain teleports onto your ship. Right next to you, in fact.

"WHAT THE HELL, BEYATCH!? WHY do you have a copy of m-", She stops suddenly. Both Leahs push you out of the room. The door shuts behind you. You hear no noise, only silence.</text>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Open the door.</text>
		<event>
			<text>Leah is standing in the middle of the room. She stares at you, unblinking, silent, with an unnatural smile on her face. The other Leah is nowhere to be found.</text>
			<choice>
				<text>Trade. Leah. Offer. Sacrifice. Beam. Special. Stock.</text>
				<event>
					<text>ACCORD. MADE.</text>
					<metaVariable name="prof_leah_deaths" op="add" val="1"/>
					<variable name="loc_nemesis" op="set" val="1"/>
					<removeCrew class="unique_leah">
						<clone>false</clone>
						<text></text>
					</removeCrew>
					<weapon name="LEAH_LIST_WEAPONS_BEAM_SPECIAL"/>
					<ship hostile="false"/>
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Continue...</text><event/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>NO NO NO NO NO NO.</text>
				<event>
					<text>You blink and suddenly the other Leah is there, clutching a hand to her chest.
					
"Damn you, Federation scum! This isn't the last you've seen of me! You beyatch and your little beyatch better watch your backs because I'm coming for you! Mwahahahah!"

She laughs before warping away. Evidently, your Leah won the fight!</text>
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Continue...</text>
						<event>
							<text>Without their leader, the rebel ship is easy pickings, and easy scrap.</text>
							<ship hostile="false"/>
							<weapon name="LOOT_KNIGHT_1"/>
							<metaVariable name="prof_leah_deaths" op="add" val="1"/>
							<variable name="loc_nemesis" op="set" val="1"/>
							<choice>
								<text>Continue...</text><event/>
							</choice>
						</event>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
        </event>
	</choice>
</event>

<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WHO_IS_WHO" unique="true">
	<ship load="SHIP_NEMESIS" hostile="true"/>
	<text>The captain hails you, revealing themselves to have obnoxiously bright blue hair and a smug glare. "Didn't expect to see m- wait, WHAT!? That's me!? I'm on your ship, but I haven't even teleported over yet!" The rebel ship's communications go blank, but then you hear a 'FWOOP' as their captain teleports onto your ship. Right next to you, in fact.

"WHAT THE HELL, BEYATCH!? WHY do you have a copy of me on your ship!?" is what you think she is trying to say, but its hard to tell over the shouting of Leah, who is also next to you.
"I didn't replace YOU with a copy of yourself, who the HELL do you think you are!?",
"Don't try to invade on MY rival, beyatch, I've had to endure days of poor cruiser management, and there's no way I'm going to lose my rival for something like this!", is what you hear before swiftly retreating out of the room.

The muffled shouting leaks through the door, until eventually, it stops. Both Leahs come out, worse for the wear.

"Beyatch, I'm your rival, ditch this beyatch so we can get on with our rivalry!"</text>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event>
			<text>"I'm the real Leah, beyatch!", "No, beyatch, I'm the real Leah, beyatch!", "Ugh! We'll never end this if you keep lying like that, beyatch!",
				
"Wait! I know! Beyatch, remember that time you shut off my ship with an EMP field using that shield generator's reactor? Now you know she's the beyatch!", "Oh come on, Delta-Base 9T-83, that one is public information! Beyatch, remember when I bought all those missiles but forgot to buy ammo for them? Now that's something the beyatch would never know!"
				
"Yeah, and your drones as well!", Leah rolls her eyes. "The Lanius! Remember when they dismantled my ship's oxygen and then I told you to help me and you did, but you also destroyed my ship in the process, you beyatch?!", "The Swarmlands! I remember bringing the Lanius from the Swarmlands! I also remember telling you to kill yourself, why didn't you listen to me, beyatch? We wouldn't be having this problem if you had!"

Both Leahs recount various adventures that you don't remember, from stories about Prodigy 43-A to failures in hacking an ASB. Ditching all her weapons for hacking, for 'advanced boarding drones', investing in 'fake mind reading', exactly 22 spiders (you killed them all, you monster beyatch!), accidental FTL drives, encounters with her 'bestie' Jerry, the list goes on and on.</text>
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Continue...</text>
				<event>
					<text>"Even that time in Chaos mode where you tried to cheat through console commands by inputting my NEMESIS_ENCOUNTER_CHAOS event, haha, I bet you never thought it would just lead to the same old fight, beyatch!"</text>
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Wait, what?</text>
						<event>
							<text>"Oh, for beyatch sake! Remember that time you flirted with me, showing me your big ass Beam! You told me you were madly in love with me! I know I said it would never work out, and it still won't, but I'll make a concession and call you my best (and only) rival! So declare me as your one and only rival and get rid of this beyatch!"

"What!? I would never bring that up willingly! Its an affront to our rivalry! That's how you know she's the beyatch! Declare ME as your one and only rival and get rid of this beyatch!"

Both Leahs implore you. It seems you must choose the right one.</text>
							<choice hidden="true">
								<text>Shoot Leah.</text>
								<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WHO_IS_WHO_CONCLUSION"/>
							</choice>
							<choice hidden="true">
								<text>Shoot Leah.</text>
								<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WHO_IS_WHO_CONCLUSION"/>
							</choice>
						</event>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
        </event>
	</choice>
</event>

<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WHO_IS_WHO_CONCLUSION" unique="true">
	<text>"Gah... You'll pay for this, Federation scum! Our rivalry is not over, will never, ever be over! Not in a million, a billion, a BEYATCH-ILLION years!"

Clutching a hand to her chest, Leah warps away. Without their leader, the rebel ship is easy pickings, and easy scrap.</text>
	<metaVariable name="prof_leah_deaths" op="add" val="1"/>
	<variable name="loc_nemesis" op="set" val="1"/>
	<ship hostile="false"/>
	<autoReward level="MED">leah_reward_special</autoReward>
	<weapon name="BEAM_1"/>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Continue...</text><event/>
	</choice>
</event>

<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_CREW" unique="true">
	<ship load="SHIP_NEMESIS" hostile="true"/>
	<text>The captain hails you, revealing themselves to have obnoxiously bright blue hair and a smug glare. "Didn't expect to see m- wait, WHAT!? That's me!? I'm on your ship, but I haven't even teleported over yet!" The rebel ship's communications go blank, but then you hear a 'FWOOP' as their captain teleports onto your ship. Right next to you, in fact.

"WHAT THE HELL, BEYATCH!? WHY do you have a copy of me on your ship!?" is what you think she is trying to say, but its hard to tell over the shouting of Leah, who is also next to you.
"I didn't replace YOU with a copy of yourself, who the HELL do you think you are!?",
"Don't try to invade on MY rival, beyatch, I've had to endure days of poor cruiser management, and there's no way I'm going to lose my rival for something like this!", is what you hear before swiftly retreating out of the room.

The muffled shouting leaks through the door, until eventually, it stops. Both Leahs come out, worse for the wear.

"Beyatch, in my infinite wisdom, I've decided to join your ship! You clearly need the help, and there's no way you can beat me while you're suffering from your.. mental issues. I know, I know, you must have missed our rivalry every hour, but an exact lookalike of me?" She shakes her head. "Shut up, beyatch, and give me access to the storage hold! We've got beams to buy, beyatch!"</text>
	<crewMember amount="1" class="unique_leah" all_skills="0">Leah</crewMember>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event>
            <text>The rebels say a tearful (?) goodbye to their leader, but not before presenting her with a gift of some scrap!</text>
            <ship hostile="false"/>
			<autoReward level="LOW">leah_reward_special</autoReward>
            <choice>
                <text>Continue...</text><event/>
            </choice>
        </event>
	</choice>
</event>

<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WEAPON" unique="true">
	<ship load="SHIP_NEMESIS" hostile="true"/>
	<text>The captain hails you, revealing themselves to have obnoxiously bright blue hair and a smug glare. "Didn't expect to see m- wait, WHAT!? That's me!? I'm on your ship, but I haven't even teleported over yet!" The rebel ship's communications go blank, but then you hear a 'FWOOP' as their captain teleports onto your ship. Right next to you, in fact.

"WHAT THE HELL, BEYATCH!? WHY do you have a copy of me on your ship!?" is what you think she is trying to say, but its hard to tell over the shouting of Leah, who is also next to you. Its hard to tell which one instigated the fight, but before you know it, they're swinging at each other. They both teleport away, and you hear a commotion somewhere else on the ship. And another, elsewhere. And then another.

Apparently, their fight is happening all over the ship. Even if you wanted to, its nigh impossible to interfere: the moment you turn towards them, they've already teleported somewhere else. One of the Leahs eventually acquiesces, clutching a hand to her chest.

"Damn you, Federation scum! This isn't the last you've seen of me! You beyatch and your little beyatch better watch your backs because I'm coming for you! Mwahahahah!"

She laughs before warping away. Evidently, your Leah won the fight!</text>
	<metaVariable name="prof_leah_deaths" op="add" val="1"/>
	<variable name="loc_nemesis" op="set" val="1"/>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event>
            <text>Without their leader, the rebel ship is easy pickings, and easy scrap.</text>
            <ship hostile="false"/>
			<autoReward level="LOW">leah_reward_special</autoReward>
			<weapon name="SHOP_ITEM_SYLVAN_BEAM_STANDARD"/>
            <choice>
                <text>Continue...</text><event/>
            </choice>
        </event>
	</choice>
</event>

